y10|n|A learning or knowing by inquiry; the knowledge of facts and events, so obtained; hence, a formal statement of such information; a narrative; a description; a written record; as, the history of a patient's case; the history of a legislative bill. ; A systematic, written account of events, particularly of those affecting a nation, institution, science, or art, and usually connected with a philosophical explanation of their causes; a true story, as distinguished from a romance; -- distinguished also from annals, which relate simply the facts and events of each year, in strict chronological order; from biography, which is the record of an individual's life; and from memoir, which is history composed from personal experience, observation, and memory.	a:2zu,69,7;18my,66,3;19lf,60,7;13n1,51,5;uug,50,5;goc,42,3;4pp,41,5;e2y,36,2;4v7,34,2;1bxz,33,6~ei,3,12;28qm,20,9;yok,31,8;1hx0,11,8;19lf,60,7;2zu,69,7;16r0,7,7;1mob,15,6;1bxz,33,6;e98,23,6	v:1qcz,45,3;4pp,28,2;27rz,22,1;n1t,21,2;1yhs,18,3;ea2,18,2;1yhk,18,1;1yhr,3,3;27b0,1,1~1qcz,45,3;1yhs,18,3;1yhr,3,3;n1t,21,2;4pp,28,2;ea2,18,2;1yhk,18,1;27b0,1,1;27rz,22,1	V:17di,5,4~17di,5,4	n:9ed,57,5;4pp,46,7;2250,37,4;e2y,36,2;1bic,34,2;nwq,32,6;qz3,32,6;s02,26,3;1qau,24,4;gjy,23,8~gjy,23,8;1mo2,10,7;273t,13,7;4pp,46,7;qz3,32,6;nwq,32,6;9ed,57,5;n2a,16,5;163a,14,5;bu1,5,4	N:15uf,40,3;20z9,27,6;8k5,18,6;21hb,16,6;1xjl,13,4;d1e,12,8;d1g,5,3~d1e,12,8;20z9,27,6;21hb,16,6;8k5,18,6;1xjl,13,4;15uf,40,3;d1g,5,3
